            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "judd"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great little appetizers and so so easy. I have been making these for 30 years. I use dill weed instead of Italian style dry dressing. Cukes on top are good. I have also put shreadded cheese and sliced black olives on top. Remember though..... these can not be made the \nnight before. The bread gets soggy."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "alhelm2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled the recipe and made these for a party and they were a huge hit! I could not find the party-sized pumpernickel bread so I used a couple of flower-shaped cookie cutters to cut shapes from regular sliced pumpernickel bread. As another reviewer suggested, I too, sprinkled dill on the top of the sandwiches. I recommend using English cucumbers, as these contain little to no seeds. If transporting to a party, these are easy to stack in a container and separate layers with parchment paper. Awesome for a party, but be sure to keep some for yourself!",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-21T13:33:06.237Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cally"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We enjoyed this recipe; however, we did not care for the small, deli appetizer size pumpernickel bread. We found it to be dry and hard, etc.\n\nSo, we got a regular loaf of pumpernickel in the bakery section of the grocery store. We like that much better; the texture is much more soft &amp; moist. One can cut this into small square s and make the same recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2018-10-11T21:31:58.440Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "hlmh23"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful! Reminded me of the cucumber sandwiches that made me feel so grown up when I finally was old enough to attend baby and bridal showers at church. If making ahead of time, I spread an almost non existent coating of butter on the bread to keep from getting soggy in the fridge. I can't stand a soggy sammy! Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2017-02-23T21:36:38.393Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Katie Myers"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was super easy! I did it just a little different. I baked the little pumpernickels into toasts and it added a fun crunch. And I alternated sprinkling them the black pepper and red pepper for and little spice :)",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-05T16:34:43.923Z"
          },
          {
